    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0988" n="868" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg868"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.00/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-09T14:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 9—1:35
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>486. My telegram number 480 December 6, 4 p.m. Superintendent Trued,<anchor
                        n="39" xml:id="d675-f1"/> Hsuchow Mission, writes Forsberg released 5th,
                    returned 6th and “Forsberg thinks Lundeen and the other foreigners will soon be
                    released,” as Government troops now pressing robbers hard.<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d675-f2"/></p>
                <p>Diplomatic body met today. Foreign Office requested further postponement
                    departure international commission. Request unanimously denied.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d675-f1" n="39" xml:id="d675-f1-content">
                <p>The Rev. Alfred E. Trued, American missionary, Augustana Synod Mission.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d675-f2" n="40" xml:id="d675-f2-content">
                <p>The Rev. Anton Lundeen was released Dec. 8, and the Rev. Einar Borg-Breen and son
                    Dec. 10. Other foreigners held were also released.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
